(forall ((p Person) (a Animal) (t Int))
  (=> (and (possesses p a t)
           (is_kind a AK_Finfish)
           (has_tail_removed a)
           (exists ((fisher Person) (t_take Int))
             (and (<= t_take t)
                  (takes fisher a t_take)
                  (on_water_body fisher
                    (as w WaterBody) t_take))))
       (or (and (has_been_finally_processed a t)
                (or (delivered_to_final_destination a t)
                    (delivered_to_certified_dealer a t)))
           (is_kind a AK_Other))))

SCHEMA_INSUFFICIENT: The schema lacks a way to associate an animal with the water body it was taken from without requiring the person to be on that water body. Additionally, there is no predicate like `taken_from_water_kind` to directly assert the water kind from which an animal was taken. I encoded this using `on_water_body fisher w t_take` with an unbound `w` constrained to be coastal, but SMT-LIB requires proper quantification. Let me provide the corrected version:

(forall ((p Person) (a Animal) (t Int))
  (=> (and (possesses p a t)
           (is_kind a AK_Finfish)
           (has_tail_removed a)
           (exists ((fisher Person) (t_take Int) (w WaterBody))
             (and (<= t_take t)
                  (takes fisher a t_take)
                  (on_water_body fisher w t_take)
                  (water_kind w WK_CoastalWater))))
       (or (and (has_been_finally_processed a t)
                (or (delivered_to_final_destination a t)
                    (delivered_to_certified_dealer a t)))
           (is_kind a AK_Other))))